WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.300
The scams Nigerians meet most, and the safe response to each.

2
00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:10.070
This is the video for module two: common scams in Nigeria and how each one works.

3
00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:21.750
The most common scams do not ask for a huge sum. Someone pretends to be your bank, your network or a government office, and asks for one small thing: a code.

4
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:25.660
Your account number is fine to share. People need it to pay you.

5
00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:39.920
But your bank will never call, SMS, email or WhatsApp you for your PIN, password, OTP, full card details or BVN. Anyone who asks is a scammer, no matter how much they know about you.

6
00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:47.400
A polite customer care agent says your BVN is suspended, and talks you through reactivation.

7
00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:53.940
While he talks, he is trying to log in to your account, or add his phone as a new device.

8
00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:57.690
The bank sends you an OTP to approve it.

9
00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:09.440
When you read it out, you approve his access. So never read out a code. CBN, EFCC and NCC staff do not phone people to collect fees or codes either.

10
00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:23.080
Funke, a POS operator in Abeokuta, gets a call. I mistakenly sent you 50,000 naira. Please send it to my brother's account, it is for hospital. She opens her own app.

11
00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:27.830
If nothing arrived, it was a fake alert. She ends the call.

12
00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:36.630
If a real credit is there, she still sends nothing. It may be stolen money, and sending it to a new account helps the thief.

13
00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:42.360
She calls her bank on the official number and reports the unexpected credit.

14
00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:51.330
And she keeps screenshots. If a transfer was a real mistake, the sender's bank contacts your bank. Let the banks handle it.

15
00:01:52.580 --> 00:02:01.140
Grace, a widow in Enugu, chatted for two months with Richard, who said he was an engineer abroad. He sent love songs every morning.

16
00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:06.290
They never had a live video call. His camera was always broken.

17
00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:14.330
Then a customs agent on WhatsApp asked her for 350,000 naira to clear a parcel of gifts.

18
00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:20.760
Her daughter searched his photo with Google Lens. The same face appeared under a different name.

19
00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:34.600
Grace blocked both numbers and reported the profiles. She lost no money. If a friend is in one, do not call her foolish. Ask gentle questions, because shame pushes people back to the scammer.

20
00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:45.750
A Ponzi scheme pays early members with newer members' money. When new money slows, it freezes withdrawals and collapses. Chioma does the sums first.

21
00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:52.880
100,000 naira at 30% becomes 130,000 after 1 month.

22
00:02:54.130 --> 00:03:01.540
About 482,700 after 6 months, and about 54 million after 24 months.

23
00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:10.360
No real business can do that. Banks and listed companies earn far less, and their returns go up and down. So Chioma declines.

24
00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:21.250
Check the company on the SEC Nigeria website, and banks on the CBN website. A CAC registration only means the business exists.

25
00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:28.380
A balance growing on an app screen is not money in your account. And never pay extra to unlock what you are owed.

26
00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:38.740
Task jobs that pay you to like videos often ask for a deposit to unlock bigger tasks. Real employers do not charge you to get a job.

27
00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:54.200
Zainab in Kano saw a blender for 28,000 naira, far below the shops. The vendor refused pay on delivery, the account name did not match, and he sent a stock photo instead of a dated video. She did not pay.

28
00:03:55.450 --> 00:04:09.610
If your line suddenly shows No service while others have signal, act fast. Call your network to block the number, then your bank to freeze transfers. Set a SIM PIN and turn on WhatsApp two-step verification.

29
00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:18.760
To remember. Never share a code. Only your app balance proves money arrived. No live video plus a crisis means scam.

30
00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:23.420
Guaranteed high returns are impossible. And never pay to get a job.

31
00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:36.340
Now practise. Save your bank's official number and time a balance check, try a Google Lens search, check one investment offer with the sums, and write your three-line emergency plan.

32
00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:38.630
Continue with the lessons below.
